## Why This Is Asked

This scenario tests knowledge of vector DB usage, chunking strategy, latency, and graceful fallback in a realistic but beginner-friendly context.

## Key Concepts

- Retrieval-augmented generation
- Document chunking
- Embedding models
- Vector DB indexing and search
- Latency targets and freshness
- Fallback mechanisms

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple chunker
function chunkText(text, maxChars) {
  const chunks = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < text.length; i += maxChars) {
    chunks.push(text.slice(i, i + maxChars));
  }
  return chunks;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle overlapping chunks to preserve context?
- How would you test latency and accuracy?

## Why This Is Asked
Examines practical system design for multilingual retrieval at scale, including chunking, embeddings, vector storage, and data provenance.

## Key Concepts
- Multilingual embeddings and cross-language retrieval
- Chunking strategies and token budgets
- Incremental updates and data provenance
- Observability, metrics, and testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-flow wiring
async function retrieve(query) {
  const e = embed(query);
  const chunks = vectorDB.search(e, topK=5);
  const ranked = rerank(chunks, query);
  return ranked.map(c => ({id: c.id, text: c.text, source: c.source}));
}
```

